# 16\. Strict Development Rules

- First inspect, then design, then implement.
- Do not replace the existing Event Platform SDK.
- Do not duplicate existing core abstractions.
- Do not make assumptions about SDK interfaces.
- Do not introduce parallel event infrastructure.
- Do not break existing modules.
- Do not modify unrelated functionality.
- Follow established naming conventions.
- Keep the implementation modular and reusable.
- Ensure compilation after each implementation phase.
- Run existing tests and add new tests.
- Resolve compilation errors before moving to the next phase.
- Do not claim functionality is implemented unless the code and tests verify it.
- If a required capability is missing, document it and propose the smallest compatible change.

