## One important architectural recommendation

I would make one additional distinction in your implementation:

- Core SDK: Knows how to publish, consume, serialize, deserialize, retry, and process events.
- Insurance domain SDK: Knows what `FNOLSubmitted`, `ClaimApproved`, and `PaymentProcessed` mean.
- Insurance application: Knows how to validate coverage, calculate settlements, assign adjusters, and process business decisions.

This separation ensures the same Event Platform SDK can later support health insurance, auto insurance, and life insurance without modifying its core functionality.

The most important first instruction to Copilot: Inspect the existing SDK and show exactly which base classes, interfaces, and modules will be extended before generating any code. This avoids creating a second event framework inside your existing platform.